  "disposition_rationale": "The batch protocol relies on air exposure for oxidation. In flow, mass transfer of oxygen from gas to liquid is the rate-limiting step for many photo-oxidations. While the batch yield is 99%, the flow residence time (5 min) is short. A 'SCREEN' disposition is appropriate because we must experimentally verify if the gas-liquid mass transfer in the selected coil is sufficient to achieve high conversion within the 5-minute residence time, or if a longer residence time or higher gas flow is required. The design is physically feasible and safe, but optimization is likely needed.",
  "proposal_json": "{\"residence_time_min\": 5.0, \"flow_rate_mL_min\": 1.0, \"temperature_C\": 21, \"concentration_M\": 0.1, \"BPR_bar\": 5, \"reactor_type\": \"photocoil\", \"tubing_material\": \"FEP\", \"tubing_ID_mm\": 1.0, \"reactor_volume_mL\": 5, \"residence_time_basis\": \"liquid_phase\", \"residence_time_inlet_min\": 5.0, \"residence_time_in_channel_min\": 5.0, \"light_setup\": \"420 nm LED, 100 mW/cm2 intensity, wrapped around coil\", \"wavelength_nm\": 420, \"streams\": [{\"stream_label\": \"Liquid Stream\", \"pump_role\": \"Syringe pump A\", \"contents\": \"Fmoc-L-methionine (0.1 M) and 4,7-diphenyl-2,1,3-benzothiadiazole (0.01 M) in Acetonitrile\", \"solvent\": \"Acetonitrile\", \"phase\": \"liquid\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": 1.0, \"concentration_M\": 0.1, \"molar_equiv\": 1.0, \"gas_flow_sccm\": 0, \"gas_flow_actual_mL_min\": 0}, {\"stream_label\": \"Gas Stream\", \"pump_role\": \"Air/O2 mass-flow controller\", \"contents\": \"Air\", \"solvent\": \"N/A\", \"phase\": \"gas\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": 0, \"concentration_M\": 0, \"molar_equiv\": 0, \"gas_flow_sccm\": 50, \"gas_flow_actual_mL_min\": 2.5}], \"mixer_type\": \"Certified gas-liquid T-mixer\", \"mixing_order_reasoning\": \"Gas and liquid are mixed immediately before the reactor to maximize interfacial area for oxygen transfer during the residence time.\", \"pre_reactor_steps\": \"1. Prepare 0.1 M solution of Fmoc-L-methionine and 10 mol% photocatalyst in acetonitrile. 2. Load into Syringe Pump A. 3. Set Air MFC to 50 sccm. 4. Set BPR to 5 bar to ensure backpressure and prevent cavitation.\", \"post_reactor_steps\": \"1. Pass through a gas-liquid separator (not in inventory, assumed available for workup) or vent gas safely. 2. Collect liquid product. 3. Analyze by HPLC/LC-MS.\", \"chemistry_notes\": \"The batch reaction uses air. In flow, we use air at 50 sccm. The gas flow is chosen to be 5x the liquid flow (in mL/min equivalent at STP) to ensure excess oxygen availability. The BPR of 5 bar increases the solubility of oxygen in the liquid phase according to Henry's Law, potentially enhancing the reaction rate compared to atmospheric pressure.\", \"stage_parameters\": {\"mixing\": \"T-mixer at 5 bar\", \"reaction\": \"5 mL FEP coil, 420 nm LED, 21 C, 5 min residence time\"}, \"reasoning_per_field\": {\"residence_time_min\": \"Matched to batch time of 5 min for initial screen.\", \"flow_rate_mL_min\": \"1.0 mL/min is well within the pump's range (0.01-5.0) and provides a reasonable throughput for a screen.\", \"reactor_volume_mL\": \"5 mL coil selected to match the 5 min residence time at 1 mL/min (V = Q * t).\", \"BPR_bar\": \"5 bar selected from available BPRs to enhance O2 solubility and maintain liquid phase.\", \"gas_flow_sccm\": \"50 sccm is a moderate flow rate, well within the MFC's 0.1-100 sccm range, providing sufficient gas-liquid contact without excessive pressure drop.\"}, \"literature_analogies\": \"Photo-oxidations of sulfides to sulfoxides are common in flow chemistry. Gas-liquid flow reactors are standard for aerobic oxidations to improve mass transfer.\", \"engine_validated\": true, \"safety_flags\": [\"Acetonitrile is flammable and toxic. Ensure proper ventilation.\", \"LED light source should be shielded to prevent eye damage.\", \"Pressurized system (5 bar) requires proper fittings and safety relief.\"], \"confidence\": 0.8}"
